  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>At 42 rue Thiers, steps from the Saint-Raphaël seafront, Moelleuses & Persillées serves French-Italian bistronomic cuisine based on fresh, local produce, centred on meats aged on site (Black Angus, Galician Blonde, Wagyu, Kobe beef). The chef, presented as a former Michelin-starred chef, adds seafood such as lobster or crustaceans; the market menu is served at lunch. The official website (mpstraphael.fr) states that the establishment "accepts dogs" and welcomes children. A terrace with a view allows outdoor dining during the season.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Hours published on the official website from 31 August: Monday and Tuesday evenings (7pm-10:30pm), Thursday, Friday and Sunday lunch (12pm-2:30pm) and evening, Saturday evening only; closed Wednesday. Book on 04 69 00 21 60 or reservation@mpstraphael.fr. The website describes a restaurant that is easy to reach, close to car parks, with gift cards and a wine list of world and local wines. The website does not say whether dogs are admitted in the dining room or only on the terrace, nor the accepted size or water bowl: ask when booking.</p>
      <p>Check before you go: the official website announces new hours since 31 August; the home page does not say whether dogs are admitted in the dining room or only on the terrace.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: if you are travelling with a good appetite and a well-behaved dog under the table, this is one of the best addresses in the area for meat.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The website places the restaurant steps from the seafront, near the town-centre car parks: enough to walk a little with your dog before or after the meal. The same establishment has an address in Bordeaux, shown at the bottom of the website page.</p>
